                <pb facs="0304" n="958" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg958"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Telegraph-line of the supreme government.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram, sent via Matamoras, December 4.
                        Received at Monterey <date calendar="gregorian" when="1873-12-04">December
                            4, 1873</date>, at 20 minutes past 4 o’clock in the
                                afternoon.]<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corpus
                                Christi.</hi></placeName></dateline></opener>
                <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Zambo Brothers</hi>: Please inform Don
                    Toribio Lozano of the following at once: A great disaster to his men and flocks;
                    seven shepherds killed; the rest not yet found: animals all lost.</p>
                <closer><signed>DIONISIO G. RAMIREZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
